speechtext:
We only had $11,000 insurance on' this. The works proposed are: Brick station, $25,000; concrete platform, $2,250; grading around station, $2,000; roundhouse, ten stalls, $50,000; turntable, foundation, ring wall, excavation, ties, &e., $3,737; turntable, 75 feet through, steel work, 102,000 lbs., $4,590; coaling pockets, 16 at $225, $3,600; ashpit, complete, including drain, $1,183; tank, complete,

$4,500; sand house, standard, $1,800; stand pipe, set up, $400; pipe from tank to stand pipe, laid, $300; earth and rock excavation 20,000 c. yds., at 75c., $15,000; earth excavation, 6,944 e. yds., at 30c., $2,083.20; rails 67 lb.,' 67 tons, at $25, $1,675; angle bars, 214 pairs, at 45c., $96.30; bolts and nuts, 856 lbs. at 4c., $34.24; track spikes, 4,500 lbs., at 3c., $135; frogs, rigid, 6 at $26.50, $159; guard rails, 6 sets at $16, $96; split points, complete, 6 sets at $45,	$270;
switch ties, 6 sets at $34, $204; switch stands, * Rampo,' 6 sets at $20, $120; track ties, 1,500 at 33c., $495; ballast, 7,000 c. yds. at 30c., $2,100; labour laying track, $313.43; freight shed, $3,500; fire pump, $1,500; engineering, inspection, advertising and contingencies, $10,850; total, $125,419.19; say $126,000, less estimated expenditure of 1912-13, $25,000, leaving $101,000. Loss to be credited to fire renewal account, $11,000; required for 1913-14, $90,000.
